2️⃣6️⃣ Flow Control

Imagine:

Sender
1000 Mbps
    ↓
Receiver
100 Mbps

Without flow control:

Receiver buffer
████████████████
      FULL

Packets may be dropped.

Flow control prevents the sender from overwhelming the receiver.


---

2️⃣7️⃣ Error Control vs Flow Control

Flow Control	Error Control

Prevents receiver overload	Handles transmission errors
Controls sending rate	Retransmits damaged/lost frames
Window-based	ACK/NAK/timeout
Protects receiver	Protects reliability



